I've implemented  Lars' suggestion to add the url of the sources.
However, source packages that generate more than one package make it
difficult to determine in which section the sources are to be found...
I hope my perl script "guesses" right most of the time.  I'll probably
implement an override for this (same goes for i386-only packages such as
lilo).

Also, if there is a non-maintainer upload of an alpha package, the
version numbers don't match up and the package is listed as out of date,
although it strictly has a higher version number. I'll rip out the
version number comparison stuff from dpkg and use that, but that will be
next week.

As before, the perl script is available at
ftp://ftp.murphy.nl/pub/debian/alpha/pauls-diff.pl in case anyone wants
to hack on it before I get round to it again.

